Z||000000||84 2in1||06-01-2001||11:18 PM||||I've just got a 1226864 comp ot of a 85 Celeberty 2.5 auto. can I use it in my 84 Fiero 2.5 M19 (4.10 4 speed) if i put the chip out of my old comp into the new one?-B-||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||06-02-2001||12:59 AM||||If it's the same part number ECM, yes. Just use the Fiero chip(s).||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-02-2001||06:29 PM||||84 uses 1226156. 1226864 is in 85-86 Fiero. <P>I'm told, but have no way to verify, that the ECM's are interchangeable.<P>In your case you need to change chips because the transmissions don't match. I don't know if you can move the chip from the 84 to the 85 ECM. You won't fry the chip but it may not run right either. Depends on just how diferant those 2 ECM's are.<P>If you have problems, You will likely need to find the 1226864 with the automatic tranny chip to get the correct responces from the ECM. Worst case, you need to see if a dealer has the correct chip or if someone can copy a known good 85-86 Fiero 2.5/auto chip.||||reg||1
